# A local marker type whose name is also a pub function of an imported
# module loses to the import when mentioned as a value.
#
# Run: kanso play bugs/marker_named_like_import.kso
#
# Should print "dropped": `drop` is declared in this file as a marker type,
# and chapter 11 says a local arm outranks an imported one on a tie. The
# bare mention `drop` should be the marker's value.
#
# Does print "something else" on both engines: the argument `drop` evaluates
# to std/list's `drop` function (it renders as <fn> when interpolated), so
# the `letter drop` arm never matches. No diagnostic is given. In a module
# directory, the import can sit in a different file (a `_test.kso` sibling)
# and still change what `drop` means in this one, so adding a test file
# changed the behaviour of the program under test.
import "std/list"

type drop

fn letter drop
  "dropped"

fn letter _
  "something else"

print (letter drop)
